module gunbc.plans.durable_work_handoff

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p, h3, cell, row }

fn durable_work_handoff_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** durable, versioned responsibility across process/unit/host/principal boundaries, with bounded admission, durable acceptance, conditional processing and attributable settlement. Ordinary in-process function calls are outside scope; local build and compilation work is in scope; a synchronous interface may use durable handoff and await its result. Proposal with owner decisions from 2026-10-12, not a landing receipt. The 2026-09-21 ruling survives at fa44b981025^:docs/plans/harness-work-lifecycle.md; it owns accepted obligations, due times and located results as durable facts, with replaceable processes and targeted wake-ups. The 2026-09-22 ruling confines the belt to wake-up delivery and bounded anti-entropy. Failed/Refused segments require recorded operator resume under the 2026-10-03 ruling."),
    p(text: "**Method/homes:** consolidate existing spellings before new modules. Factor shared standings/dispatch/completion out of v2.std.demand_engine into std.work_queue; std.durable_handoff adds durability; gunbc.durable_handoff_host realizes it once for host services. Compose durable_exclusive_hold, durable_compare_and_set.CasGeneration/CasExpectation, temporal_effect.stall_budget_verdict, effects.IdempotencyEvidence, upsert_decision/realization_reconcile/goal_assessment and std.decision. The queue holds obligations and evidence, never a valuation or fixed preference; selection under the demand’s declared objective decides order, retry, wait/move/supply and expiry."),
    p(text: "**Item/state:** key = obligation kind + subject, content-addressed where applicable; every entry/wake-up/hold/receipt uses it and names product.fabric.demand.Demand. Outstanding work derives from durable subject evidence under the running revision, never a separate flag. Thus deploy/revision change is an event even without new evidence. Closed standings: Ready; Waiting(on named event/time/unread observation); Running(exclusive hold); RetryDue(at,cause,attempt); Stopped(cause,owner); Finished(Completed | Cancelled(by) | Exhausted(cause)). Waiting without a source and Stopped without an owner are unconstructible. Stopped is resumable dead letter; exhaustion is terminal and cannot be reset by resume. Unread evidence is unknown: Waiting or a defect-owned Stopped, never Ready/Finished/empty fleet."),
    p(text: "**DemandState map:** Waiting/Ready/Running become the shared standings; DemandAvailable retains its value-carrying wrapper with Finished.Completed standing, whose dependents the engine releases. DemandRefused becomes owned Stopped. Capacity/lookup DemandBlocked causes become Waiting; cycles/missing edges/key conflict/refused prerequisite become Stopped. Unconstructed DemandLeasePending/DemandSuspended/DemandCommitPending delete in M0; their future needs return as named Waiting causes. Domain records such as WorkflowSegmentState/AttemptState/CallerWorkPhase remain and project shared standing; they are not mechanically deleted."),
    p(text: "**Wake-ups/queue:** hints carry only keys; duplicates coalesce and reordered hints rederive state. Sources are Arrival, Completion (same item plus direct dependents), RevisionChange, DueTime, OperatorAction and Resync. Each service declares every evidence change that can make its kinds owed. Enqueue is atomic, create-only and idempotent. Admission follows selected order with identity tie-break last; concurrency is granted leases, not service constants. Every demand declares maximum wait or explicit none; exceeding a maximum makes an order infeasible. With feasible order and bounded steps, ready work is claimed within that bound; unbounded-wait work is still reconsidered at every capacity event. Holds recover only on observed holder death, never age, and stale CasGeneration claims refuse."),
    p(text: "**Worker/settlement:** claim→rederive→run next eligible ensure→persist result immediately→settle. Choices use select→ensure→independent observation. Advanced enqueues Completion for item/dependents; Finished records completed/attributable cancelled/exhausted; Waiting parks on its source; RetryAfter(at,cause) requires a retry law; Stopped names cause/owner; Transferred(to,ref) records another queue’s accepted responsibility. Delivery acknowledgment, execution-resource release and history retention are separate: releasing a hold never erases recovery evidence. Receiver durably accepts before sender records transfer; generalize capture_chunk.LocalCommitStanding/DownstreamAcceptanceStanding so both views join."),
    p(text: "**Retry:** per-implementation law establishes admissibility and earliest time only; objective selection chooses then/later/elsewhere/stop. Earliest time increases exponentially with jitter and upstream retry-after can only raise it. Bounds cover whole history across restart/resume/new endpoint; only actual work outcomes count and healthy probes never reset a failing series. Cancellation/exhaustion persist, never follow from silence. RetryAfter without a law refuses; the proposal maps it to Stopped, while whether that remains the universal default is explicitly still an owner question."),
    p(text: "**Resync/health:** bounded anti-entropy enqueues keys, never performs work. Persist a wrapping cursor over an evidence-derived unfinished-subject index maintained by settlements, so cost follows outstanding work rather than history. Count owed-but-unqueued items by missing source as lost wake-ups. Health exposes depth by standing, oldest owed age, stopped/exhausted causes and ownership, lost wake-ups and consumer-start failures. A consumer that cannot start is an owned Stopped queue member. Generalize event_backlog_judge and unit_standing to every queue consumer; the served page renders this one reading."),
    p(text: "**Objective interface (agreed with flex-inference):** AdmissionTerms carries DemandObjective(profile declaration, valuations); price money, delay per second, interruption per event and accepted-work unit in one account. Explicit zero stays present; missing terms refuse. Budget caps remain in BuyTerms and maximum wait in AdmissionTerms, projected into hard constraints. select_realization’s proposed ValuedObjective(identity,valuations) runs after hard constraints/Pareto and minimizes valued sum, identity tie-break last; profile is receipt authority. Until it exists, existing policies yield SelectionNeedsPolicy, never a stub. Queue-owned decision subjects are dispatch, retry and keep-waiting/cancel expiry; flex owns wait/move/acquire supply via select_supply→select_realization. Expiry needs declared deadline valuation or maximum wait, no queue default."),
    p(text: "**Policy-switch witness:** fixed work/resources, two demand profiles and a planted tradeoff must change dispatch, supply and expiry without code edits. A dominating candidate wins under both profiles while receipts retain their different policy authorities, so indiscriminate flipping fails. Retry choice is likewise selected, distinct from admissibility. Services author only kinds/evidence dependency order, retry law, wake-up sources, run bounds and resync cadence/bounds; they do not own economic preferences."),
    p(text: "**Host realization:** generalize roadmap_attempt_exit_spool’s atomic entries, AttemptExitSpoolStage and claim/settle/running-reconcile operations over an entry codec. DirectoryNotEmpty path units provide level-triggered delivery; transient worker unit names realize holds; one timer per queue serves due times/resync. Workers use an admitted work slice, not a serving slice (#13795). Fabric-store realization can later inhabit the same interface."),
    p(text: "**Consolidation A–C:** A deletes unused workflow.types, approval_broker WorkClaim/TakeoverAdmission, host_converge SpawnRetryBackstop and orphan fleet service/timer/cadence vocabulary once no caller remains in the change's closure (the caller census is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`)). B consolidates occupancy at durable_exclusive_hold, liveness at DurableHoldHolderLiveness with one InvocationID systemd observer, stale-holder law at ReleaseLaw and fencing at CasGeneration; unit/tmux/flock/exclusive-create/git-ref mechanisms become realizations. Merge temporal/ProcessLeasePlan/DispatchLeasePlan decision folds; CAS/event chains/capacity pools/single-use grants/rentals/GitHub concurrency remain distinct contracts. Age-based recovery cases require operator rulings. C replaces BeltPassOutcome/BeltObligationEnqueue/PublicationHelperDisposition with shared settlement and corrects not-yet refusals and unknown/refusal→done misclassifications."),
    p(text: "**Consolidation D–F:** D unifies exit/publication spools under create-only enqueue, capture acceptance pair, health and every consumer unit; publication answers enqueue their attempt directly. E chooses one instant authority, unifies retry for harness_placement_rounds/WorkspaceConsumerRetry/publication re-ask/Spark transfer, splits belt_tick_run_bound by kind, repoints stall readings and deletes RetryCount with its mirror. F removes serving_delay_valuation placeholders/literal-zero substitutes and fixed warm/roster/CAS/retry/concurrency preferences in favor of demand selections. attempt_lifecycle’s recovery deadline only admits contenders; CAS chooses the holder. approval_broker.ExecutionObligation has no executor in the audit and is not a migration target until one exists."),
    p(text: "**Milestones/acceptance:** owning consolidation wave precedes each new home. M0 changes the model before consumers; RED duplicate enqueue, max-wait violation, stale fence, source-less Waiting, owner-less Stopped, lawless retry/restart-bound reset and resync prefix starvation. M1 migrates belt on lab: revision/completion/due sources, cursor index, proper verification-window Waiting, selected decisions and visible health. Execute a declared N dispatches without hand steps, one attempt reaches its PR while another is stopped, killed controller resumes without user action, no lost wake-ups in those runs and the profile switch changes a planted tradeoff. M2 makes publication a queue/Transferred settlement and exposes start failures; retire publication drops by their own triggers. M3 migrates compute recovery, workspace consumer, runner cells and fleet converge by replacement/deletion, not adapters."),
    p(text: "**Caller/conformance:** caller_backlog projects CallerWorkRecord to item, budget.fence_admits grant generation to fence, WorkWaiting to Ready/Waiting/Running, completed/cancelled/recovery-bound-exceeded to the three Finished terminals. A synchronous serving path is in scope; “no server queue” is a realization choice to revisit, not exclusion. Add the durable-handoff conformance_domains row only after homes exist and M1 consumes them, with operator sign-off because it changes reviewer scope. Review bounded acceptance, complete wake-up sources, closed standing, objective-selected choices, lawful retries and visible health; reject silent loops, prefix-only scans, ownerless failure, age recovery and duplicate hold/dedup/dead-letter/time vocabularies. [Original specimens and ladder](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/durable_work_handoff.dag) are dated evidence. Lost-wake counting is mitigation; only one durable evidence+entry append makes that guarantee structural. Fenced claims, admitted worker placement and constructed standings likewise require execution, not this proposal."),
    h3(text: "Granted work program — operator-approved sequence"),
    p(text: "This extends the durable handoff authority above; it is the one program design, not a second build queue or a deployment receipt. gunbc build, compile, test and run submit canonical work through durable acceptance, selection, grant issuance, execution and reconciliation. Local execution cuts over to this final route before any remote host. Cargo is an internal producer inside a grant. Generic arbitrary-command remote compatibility is not the service contract."),
    p(text: "Identity (PR 2): product.fabric.work.SourceManifestRef identifies the exact source content manifest. A clean Git tree and a dirty worktree are adapters into that same identity, with provenance separate. Preserve declared roots, entry, operation, dependencies, outputs, target architecture, flags and relevant environment in the canonical work identity. Declared toolchain requirements remain separate from the observed toolchain receipt; observation cannot silently rewrite the request. Reuse WorkKey, ExecutionAttemptKey and std.computation_identity rather than minting parallel keys."),
    p(text: "Selection and grant (PR 4): std.decision selects a satisfying offer and records an attributable decision, including evidence and policy. It does not issue launch permission. A separate grant authority composes product.fabric.execution.ExecutionGrant only after cell and host resource reservations and the executor permit have committed. Exactly one grant binds an attempt and lease generation. gunbc.compute.host_capacity is a host-scoped resource ledger behind that grant, never a launcher. Parent and child holds are ingredients, not permission. Interrupted partial reservation stays charged and reconciles; it cannot expose a grant. Preserve the existing fabric conservation contract: the canonical grant transition commits all required ledgers or none; a sequential physical realization must prove that contract, not rename a partial commit atomic."),
    p(text: "Executor contract (PR 5): local systemd and microVM are profiles of one interface, not interchangeable isolation classes. Each request declares architecture, toolchain, isolation class, network policy, secrets policy, storage/artifact obligations and resource bounds. Selection excludes offers that do not satisfy every requirement before ranking. A resident executor consumes the committed grant, verifies its binding and returns terminal evidence. SSH converges the host; it does not submit or launch individual work. The microVM revision-job chain retains its owning provisioning and root-approval authority; no fixed VM/root route is imposed on every request."),
    p(text: "Durable attempt controller (PR 3): acceptance precedes dispatch. A fenced claim lease owns transitions and attempt minting, with at most one live attempt per request. Waiting names a wake source; capacity-full waits for release and does not consume execution retry budget. Wait, reselect and terminal refusal are explicit transitions. Reselection creates a new decision record. Restart recovers durable intent, launch acknowledgment and receipt evidence; a lost acknowledgment is not proof of no launch. Reconcile lost launch or lost receipt with the executor before retry. No second attempt launches until the first cell is proved not running. An unreachable cell retains its reservations and enters named Waiting or owned Stopped; silence and lease age never prove quiescence. Cancellation persists intent, requests termination and reconciles terminal evidence. OOM retry is a second typed attempt admitted under the retry law and a new grant, never a hidden shell retry."),
    p(text: "Outcomes and receipts: extend gunbc.compute.work_request.WorkOutcome for the domain result and terminal evidence, including KilledByWatchdog { reason, observed activity, last progress, window, termination receipt }. A watchdog kill is not a compile/test failure. The execution receipt is distinct: extend product.fabric.execution.Receipt and its ExecutionReceipt payload to bind the outcome to attempt, complete lease identity and generation, source and work identity. Reject stale or mismatched receipts without completing a different request. These extensions are PR 3/5 obligations, not implemented declarations in this design."),
    p(text: "Settlement is plural: proved descendant/cell quiescence permits resource release; request completion, result publication and history retention remain separate facts. A leader exit, inactive unit or receipt arrival alone does not release descendants. Preserve recovery evidence after release. Publication failure retries publication under its law, not execution. A retained result is reattachment to the same request, not reuse of an effectful result for a new request."),
    p(text: "Acceptance/REST: integrate #15310 durable acceptance and readback, now owned with PR 3 by bold-dove-340. Persist request identity before PUT /requests/{id}; GET reconciles that identity. Same identity with different payload refuses. The CLI prints accepted, unknown or rejected and the stable authenticated resource URL after the submission response. Lost response means unknown, not cancellation or rejection. Acceptance is durable before acknowledgment and dispatch. Initial CLI scope remains submit-and-print; a gate must observe an admitted terminal receipt before publishing a verdict. This does not promise exactly-once external effects."),
    p(text: "Preparation and secrets: preparation itself is admitted work before source/archive/vendor effects. Preserve #15374 separate unprivileged preparer and artifact writer, verified store-owned copies, create-only publication, protected inputs and declared pathname-ancestry limitation. Reconcile these with the chosen executor profile before implementation; do not assume a previously described account install is live. Each executor receives only the credential scoped to its attempt. Check-publishing identity stays on the light runner, outside checked-out PR code. No fork-PR access to the shadow service."),
    p(text: "Caches remain with std.materialization_provider, std.artifact_store and sccache through gunbc.ci.ci_materialization. An executor declares which providers it reaches; selection may read reachability and warmth as evidence but owns no cache. Complete identity and admitted effect contracts govern reuse. No shared mutable Cargo target between attempts; cache loss recomputes without changing verdict. Existing caching limits below remain limits, not promised deployment."),
    h3(text: "Ordered cuts and executing acceptance"),
    p(text: "PR 0: Split #15830 worker-session cap from compute policy; preserve existing compute ceiling and pool behavior exactly."),
    p(text: "PR 1: This design refresh; no provider code. Record owners, unresolved integration and first-host decision."),
    p(text: "PR 2: Canonical work/source identity adapters; dirty and clean representations of equal bytes agree, changed declared input changes identity, observed toolchain mismatch refuses."),
    p(text: "PR 3: Durable attempt controller; restart/cancel/lost-launch/lost-receipt controls demonstrate one live attempt and fenced reconciliation."),
    p(text: "PR 4: Host reservations plus separate grant issuance; concurrent demand cannot double-spend parent capacity, failed reservation/permit cannot mint launch authority."),
    p(text: "PR 5: Granted executor contract and local systemd realization; actual passing/failing work, watchdog/OOM evidence, descendant quiescence and second-attempt retry controls."),
    p(text: "PR 6: Local end-to-end cutover deletes BOTH direct compute_provide launch and worker bin/gunbc shell bypass. validate_worktree and all build consumers use the final granted route. A planted bypass must fail; caller/controller restart must preserve accepted responsibility."),
    p(text: "PR 7: First remote host executor/admission after local cutover; resident executor, SSH convergence only. Operator host decision and live consumer permit are prerequisites."),
    p(text: "PR 8: Two-candidate selection and remote recovery; differing admissible offers exercise policy choice, reselection records a new decision, unreachable first cell cannot duplicate execution."),
    p(text: "PR 9: Separate OPTIONAL remote-build-shadow CI job. Operator explicitly approved this job-roster addition. It does not own the required verdict. No fork-PR access or service credential exposed to PR code; run the finite matrix below."),
    p(text: "PR 10: Stage existing CI capacity onto the service: withdraw old admission, quiesce all old work, then republish to service admission BEFORE switching verdict. Prove no overlapping authority or lost charged reservation."),
    p(text: "PR 11: Switch v2-bootstrap verdict to the admitted service receipt. Rollback withdraws new admission and proves quiescence before restoring the old CI capacity authority; never run both authorities over the same capacity. Keep receipt and source binding on the light runner."),
    p(text: "PR 12: Delete ctrl-build/BuildBuddy integration, credential/env dispatch and remaining compatibility, then widen admitted consumers. The active direct compute and worker shell bypasses already disappeared at PR 6; this is not permission to retain them until PR 12."),
    h3(text: "Finite shadow acceptance matrix"),
    p(text: "Each case runs through real acceptance, controller, grant and executor, retaining request/attempt/source/lease identities, binary/toolchain observations and quiescence evidence. Success: declared outputs and success receipt publish only for the bound request. Expected compile/test failure: domain failure publishes without infrastructure retry or a green verdict. Generated changes: declared artifacts and diff bind the source; no silent working-tree mutation is discarded. Cancellation: persisted cancel intent leads to termination evidence before release. OOM: typed infrastructure outcome, no compile-failure substitution; any lawful retry has a new attempt/grant. Executor restart: reconcile persisted launch/result without duplicate execution. Stale receipt: reject old lease or wrong source/attempt and leave the current request unaffected. Unreachable cell: retain charge and uncertainty; no second launch until independently proved stopped. Each control names the mutation that would make it red before PR 9 can count it as acceptance."),
    h3(text: "Sibling dispositions and ownership"),
    p(text: "Disposition here means the intended program boundary, not a claim that integration has executed. Unfinished reconciliation is tracked by gunbc.integration_concern durable_work_program_boundaries. #15392 integrated into PR 10: capacity writer cutover and captured generations preserve old obligations while admission changes. #15368 integrated into PR 4: parent reservations feed the separate grant, never authorize launch. #15374 integrated into PR 2/5: preparation principals and protected artifact storage inhabit the executor contract. Keep these three PRs open for their owning cuts, not competing plans."),
    p(text: "#15310 integrated: merged acceptance/REST is the existing request boundary consumed by PR 3, owner bold-dove-340. validate_worktree/compute_provide integrated into PR 6, owner quick-newt-573 (quiet-dove-609 archived; #15839 merged). MicroVM revision jobs distinct-with-reason: profile-specific isolation/provisioning and root approvals remain, while execution consumes the common grant contract; owner quick-newt-573, successor to crisp-ibex-490. fabric_control_plane.CellReservation distinct-with-reason: cell occupancy, composed behind the grant, not host resource accounting. runner_slot_allocation distinct-with-reason: runner-slot lifecycle; withdraw/quiesce/republish its capacity at PR 10 rather than create a second work scheduler. #15313 patient requests distinct-with-reason: post-delivery standing, not accepted execution ownership. ctrl-build/BuildBuddy deleted in PR 12; no generic-command compatibility service survives."),
    p(text: "bold-dove-340 owns PR 1 and PR 3 durable lifecycle, including #15310 acceptance. quick-newt-573 owns the program, local executor, host bring-up, CI migration and the successor surfaces above. The program owner dispatches other cuts to their owning lanes and creates missing source-manifest, grant-composition and host_capacity ownership. This plan does not dispatch work into another lane. Closure of a session does not close its integration obligation."),
    h3(text: "First remote host — open operator decision needed by PR 7"),
    p(text: "Butch is fail-closed per keeper calm-crab-645: GPU endpoints are vanishing with unresolved cause, no qualifying boot is planned, console has not attested the host key, and the account is ubuntu@. srv3/srv4 are operator-limited to sporadic builds: placement refuses while ANY DIMM is above 85 C; the thermal plan is open. srv2 is unassessed. These are decision inputs, not approved capacity. Consumer-owned permits plus live-condition admission (including the DIMM gate) authorize eligibility, never a host allowlist. Host selection is not needed to land PR 1, and reopening a host alone does not issue an execution grant."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Current caching support"), cell(text: "Decision / standing")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Rust compilation"), cell(text: "Existing compute provider configures shared sccache; reuse this infrastructure for eligible compilations. Its writable Cargo target is deleted after settlement, so persistent Cargo incremental targets are not current cross-request support.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Exact build/native products"), cell(text: "Existing compute materialization stores and native product caches can reuse verified exact outputs. Native-product caching is explicitly enabled and has limited consumers; shared-tier availability requires credentials and live validation. Reuse these authorities rather than inventing another store.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: ".dag preparation"), cell(text: "The floor/seed shares indexes and typed-module caches within a process. This is not general persisted cross-process incremental compilation; retain supported reuse without promising a new incremental compiler.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Test/run results"), cell(text: "Do not generally cache executions: return the retained result when reattaching to the same request, but a new effectful or measurement request executes anew. Any hermetic result reuse must follow its existing declared identity/effect contract.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Revision-job VM"), cell(text: "Currently builds in a fresh work disk; host build caches are not wired into that path. Connecting the existing artifact/sccache mechanisms is implementation work, not already-deployed cache support. Begin there; persistent writable incremental snapshots are not a prerequisite for the first service.")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "Cache compatibility is determined by exact inputs, dependencies, compiler/toolchain, target ABI and relevant options/environment. Cache loss causes recomputation, not a changed verdict. Correctness never depends on writable cache state; concurrent requests do not share a mutable target directory. PR 6 removes direct local dispatch after the local final route passes its controls; PR 12 deletes the remaining legacy transport integration. Local is an explicitly selected executor profile, never an implicit fallback."),
  ]
}

data durable_work_handoff_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "durable-work-handoff",
  title: "Durable work handoff: the event-queue conformance pattern",
  body: durable_work_handoff_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this document when std.durable_handoff and its host realization carry these rules in their own declarations and witnesses, the named program consumers use the granted route with the finite acceptance controls executed, sibling integration concerns have evidence-backed dispositions, and the durable-handoff conformance row has landed under its approval rule.") },
}
